@startuml
title BERA - Multi-market Search Core (Implementation PR A)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "Application - PR A" {
  class SearchIntent {
    +original_user_query: str
    +display_limit: int
    +selected_providers
    +generation: int
    +requested_geographic_scopes
  }

  class AcquisitionBudgetPolicy {
    +MAX_DISPLAY_LIMIT
    +supported_display_limits
    +acquisition_budget(provider, display_limit)
    +maximum_internal_acquisitions(provider)
    +validate_display_limit()
    +create_plan()
    +validate_plan()
  }

  class ProviderBudgetRule {
    +maximum_internal_acquisitions: int
    +maximum_acquisition_budget: int
    +candidate_buffer_multiplier: int
  }

  class BoundedAcquisitionPlan {
    +provider
    +acquisition_budget
    +maximum_internal_acquisitions
    +steps
    +requested_geographic_scope
    +complete_effective_geographic_scope
    +partial_effective_geographic_scope
    +allow_early_termination
  }

  class InternalAcquisitionStep {
    +key
    +candidate_limit
    +required_for_complete_coverage
  }

  class AcquisitionBatch {
    +candidates
    +fetched
    +mapped
    +rejected
  }

  class ProviderRunMetrics {
    +display_requested
    +acquisition_budget
    +acquisition_requested
    +fetched
    +mapped
    +rejected
    +usable
    +displayed
  }

  enum ProviderStatus {
    SUCCESS
    EMPTY
    ERROR
  }

  enum CoverageStatus {
    COMPLETE
    PARTIAL
  }

  class ProviderRunResult {
    +provider
    +generation
    +status
    +ordered_usable_pool
    +canonical_session_results
    +metrics
    +requested_geographic_scope
    +effective_geographic_scope
    +coverage_status
  }

  class SearchSessionSnapshot {
    +intent
    +provider_results
    +settled
    +has_incidents
    +completion_label
    +commit(result)
  }

  class "execute_bounded_provider_search()" as LogicalSearch
}

package "Existing Application / Provider Boundary" {
  interface ExistingProviderOperation {
    +execute(...)
  }
  interface ProviderPort {
    +search(...)
  }
}

package "GUI / Orchestration" {
  class TrackerState {
    +start_search()
    +coordinate()
    +serialize_for_ui()
  }
}

AcquisitionBudgetPolicy --> ProviderBudgetRule : owns rules
AcquisitionBudgetPolicy --> BoundedAcquisitionPlan : create_plan / validate_plan
BoundedAcquisitionPlan --> InternalAcquisitionStep : contains *
SearchIntent --> LogicalSearch
BoundedAcquisitionPlan --> LogicalSearch
AcquisitionBudgetPolicy --> LogicalSearch : required at execute
LogicalSearch --> ExistingProviderOperation : composes bounded calls
ExistingProviderOperation --> ProviderPort
ExistingProviderOperation --> AcquisitionBatch
LogicalSearch --> ProviderRunMetrics : aggregates
LogicalSearch --> ProviderRunResult : produces
ProviderRunResult --> ProviderRunMetrics
ProviderRunResult --> ProviderStatus
ProviderRunResult --> CoverageStatus
SearchIntent --> SearchSessionSnapshot
ProviderRunResult --> SearchSessionSnapshot : immutable commit
TrackerState --> SearchIntent : creates / coordinates
TrackerState --> LogicalSearch : orchestrates
TrackerState --> SearchSessionSnapshot : owns current snapshot

note right of ProviderRunResult
  Result owns its generation.
  A stale result cannot be relabelled by the caller.
end note

note right of SearchSessionSnapshot
  commit(result) validates:
  result.generation == intent.generation
end note

note right of ProviderRunMetrics
  Invariants:
  displayed = min(usable, display_requested)
  usable = len(ordered_usable_pool)
  displayed = len(canonical_session_results)
end note

note right of AcquisitionBudgetPolicy
  Canonical source of truth for:
  display limits
  acquisition_budget
  maximum internal acquisitions
  Executable plans must be derived from
  or validated against this policy.
end note

note bottom of LogicalSearch
  One logical provider search may compose multiple bounded existing operations.
  It MUST NOT start a second logical search merely to refill rejected/mapping-lost candidates.
end note

note right of AcquisitionBatch
  PR A batch contract is candidates plus optional
  fetched/mapped/rejected counts.
  Effective geographic scope is NOT a batch field.
  Coverage is derived from BoundedAcquisitionPlan
  onto ProviderRunResult only.
end note

note right of ExistingProviderOperation
  Preserve low-level contracts.
  Example: Facebook execute() = one Actor run
end note

note right of TrackerState
  TrackerState coordinates.
  Do NOT move:
  provider strategy
  budget policy
  deduplication
  domain rules
  into TrackerState.
end note

package "Deferred staged work" {
  class "PR B\nPositional comparison" as PRB
  class "PR C\nProvider diagnostics" as PRC
  class "PR D\nQuery routing + Venezuela scope" as PRD
  class "PR E\nCSV/currency/lifecycle/browser gate" as PRE
}

PRB ..> SearchSessionSnapshot : later consumer
PRC ..> ProviderRunMetrics : later instrumentation/UI
PRD ..> SearchIntent : later routing/scope integration
PRD ..> BoundedAcquisitionPlan : later concrete geo plans
PRE ..> SearchSessionSnapshot : later export/lifecycle
@enduml
